    {
      "filename": "Hardknott Castle Roman Fort - Bathhouse - geograph.org.uk - 546609.jpg",
      "title": "File:Hardknott Castle Roman Fort - Bathhouse - geograph.org.uk - 546609.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Hardknott_Castle_Roman_Fort_-_Bathhouse_-_geograph.org.uk_-_546609.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hardknott_Castle_Roman_Fort_-_Bathhouse_-_geograph.org.uk_-_546609.jpg",
      "width": 640,
      "height": 480,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Rob Farrow",
      "description": "Hardknott Castle Roman Fort - Bathhouse. The bathhouse consisted of five parts, a plunge pool, the \"Frigidarium\" (cold room), \"Tepidarium\" (warm room) and \"Caldarium\" (hot room). These four rooms made up the rectangular building in the forefront and are listed from left to right as seen. Behind them is a separate round room the 546613 properly known as a \"Laconicum\". For a plan see 546616",
